---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO, getBase } from '../consts';

const title = 'Terms of Service · Udaan';
const description = "Terms for using Udaan: what it is, how the AI features work, the MIT license, and the usual no-warranty disclaimer.";
const lastUpdated = 'September 17, 2026';
const base = getBase(import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-16 pb-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-muted uppercase">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose mt-8">
      <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms cover the Udaan desktop application, the web build, and this marketing site
        (together, the "Services"), published by Pranav Raut. By downloading, installing, or using
        Udaan, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, don't use the Services.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What Udaan is</h2>
      <p>
        Udaan is free, open-source software that helps you tailor a resume and cover letter to a job
        description using an AI provider you configure. It is local-first: there is no account to
        create, and your data is stored on your own device. Source code is published at
        <a href={REPO} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/Pranavraut033/resume-builder</a>
        under the MIT License (see
        <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/LICENSE`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LICENSE</a>);
        third-party components carry their own licenses, listed in-app under Settings → Third-Party
        Licenses, including resume templates adapted from
        <a href="https://github.com/Afif718/Resumify" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resumify</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. No account, nothing to terminate</h2>
      <p>
        Because there's no Udaan account or server-side login, there's nothing for us to suspend or
        terminate. If you connect an optional third-party integration (an AI provider's API key, or
        Gmail), you control that connection entirely from Settings and can disconnect it at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>4. AI-generated content</h2>
      <p>
        Tailored resumes, cover letters, ATS analysis, and any other AI-generated output are produced
        by the AI provider you chose, based on the prompts Udaan sends on your behalf. AI output can be
        wrong, incomplete, or inconsistent with your actual experience even when it reads confidently.
        <strong>You are responsible for reviewing and verifying anything you submit to an employer</strong> —
        Udaan and its author make no representation that generated content is accurate, truthful, or
        will produce any particular outcome in a job application.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Using an AI provider, the optional managed provider, or the optional Gmail integration means
        you're also bound by that third party's own terms (your AI provider's terms of service, Google's
        terms, Stripe's terms for the managed provider's payments). We don't control those services and
        aren't responsible for their availability, pricing, or behavior. See the
        <a href={`${base}privacy`}>Privacy Policy</a> for how each of these is actually used.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Don't use Udaan to generate content that's fraudulent, defamatory, or that misrepresents
        credentials, qualifications, or work history you don't actually have. Don't use it to violate
        any AI provider's or Google's acceptable-use policies, or to violate applicable law. Don't
        attempt to reverse-engineer or abuse the managed provider's metering to obtain service beyond
        what you've paid for.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The Services are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, express
        or implied, including any warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or
        non-infringement. We don't warrant that the Services will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that
        any AI output will be accurate.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, the author of Udaan is not liable for any indirect,
        incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of the Services,
        including damages related to a job application outcome, data loss, or a third-party service
        (AI provider, Google, Stripe) being unavailable or behaving unexpectedly.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the product changes. Material changes will be noted in the
        <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">changelog</a>
        along with the "Last updated" date above. Continuing to use Udaan after an update means you
        accept the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: open an issue on
        <a href={`${REPO}/issues`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
